## Local development

```bash
mvn spring-boot:run
```
[[- if or (has "database") (has "messaging") ]]

`compose.yaml` describes the backing services. Spring Boot starts them with Docker Compose
when you run the app locally, so Docker must be running. Tests use Testcontainers, which also
needs Docker.
[[- end ]]

Run the tests with:

```bash
mvn test
```

The service exposes `GET /api/v1/ping` on port `8080`, plus `/actuator/health` and
`/actuator/prometheus`.
[[- if has "openapi" ]] The API documentation is served at `/swagger-ui.html`.[[ end ]]
[[- if or (has "database") (has "messaging") ]]

## Configuration in production

Point the service at real infrastructure with environment variables:
[[ if or (has "postgresql") (has "mysql") ]]
- `SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL`, `SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME`, `SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD`
[[- end ]]
[[- if has "mongodb" ]]
- `SPRING_DATA_MONGODB_URI`
[[- end ]]
[[- if has "kafka" ]]
- `KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS`
[[- end ]]
[[- if has "rabbitmq" ]]
- `SPRING_RABBITMQ_HOST`, `SPRING_RABBITMQ_USERNAME`, `SPRING_RABBITMQ_PASSWORD`
[[- end ]]
[[- end ]]
[[- if has "flyway" ]]

Database migrations live in `src/main/resources/db/migration` and run on startup.
[[- end ]]
